    },
    {
      "headline": "Sulyok loses Holy Crown vote, presidency future uncertain as Tisza holds removal power",
      "summary": "President Tamás Sulyok's proposal to move the Holy Crown of Hungary to the parliament's plenary chamber for the incoming MPs' oath was blocked by the Holy Crown Council, in a symbolic defeat ahead of the transfer of power. Separately, media and legal commentators debated whether Magyar would seek Sulyok's removal given the Tisza supermajority, while a pro-Sulyok petition attracted fewer than 100,000 signatures despite Orbán amplifying it. Sulyok also pre-emptively signed off several decisions before the government handover, including awarding a state decoration to Trócsányi László."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Index newspaper forced to publish court-ordered correction admitting its Fidesz-era 'Tisza tax plan' articles were false",
      "summary": "Index.hu, regarded as a government-aligned outlet, published a court-ordered correction admitting that documents it had promoted during the election campaign as the Tisza Party's tax plan were not, in fact, Tisza's documents and that no valid conclusions could be drawn from them. Magyar publicly demanded a front-page correction displayed for days, describing the original articles as the 'biggest lies' of the campaign. The court had previously ordered the correction and Index also owed HUF 500,000 in legal costs."
    }
  ]
